// SF (store forwarding) -- the RA-vs-WRA separating behaviour, second shape.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: RA strictly weaker than WRA.
// Source: Lahav & Boker, TOPLAS 2022, Ex. 3.7 (SF).
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/RA-vs-WRA/SF.
//
// A thread writes x = 1, reads x = 2 from the other thread, then reads x = 1
// again -- its own earlier write, now stale. RA and SRA forbid it by
// read-coherence. WRA allows it, which is why WRA validates the store-forwarding
// optimisation that rewrites the second read to the constant 1; the paper notes
// that same rewrite is UNSOUND for RA and SRA, since it would then yield this
// outcome even under SC.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA ALLOWS. RA, SRA, C11, RC11 and SC FORBID.
x := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel);
  r0 := x.load(acq);
  r1 := x.load(acq)
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rel)
}
%%
forbid (r0 = 2 && r1 = 1) [RA]
